------------------------------------------------------------------------------
phase A: RDCFG latency by STALLWAIT on the Configuration Unit (C12/CFGEXU)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  BlackholeA0 STALLWAIT.md, condition C12: "Any thread has an instruction in
  any stage of the Configuration Unit pipeline", with block bit B7 (inside
  STALL_THREAD) "Block thread from starting new Configuration Unit
  instructions". BlackholeA0 RDCFG.md: "After issuing one or more `RDCFG`
  instructions, software is encouraged to use `STALLWAIT` to wait for the
  Configuration Unit to no longer be busy."
  Predicted from ConfigurationUnit.md's stage table: RDCFG holds stage 0 then
  stage +1, RMWCIB holds stage 0 alone, so the difference is >= 1 cycle/pair.

  variant thr        rdcfg      rmwcib      setdma   d(rmwcib)   d(setdma)
  t1      1          2.968       2.968       2.968      +0.000      -0.000

  bare occupancies (must agree, or the difference is occupancy):
    RDCFG 0.998   RMWCIB0 0.998   SETDMAREG 0.998

TTBENCH_CFGLAT_OCC: 0.9978 0.9979 0.9979
TTBENCH_CFGLAT_STALLCOST: 1.9704
TTBENCH_CFGLAT_COND: C12 CFGEXU 0x1000
TTBENCH_CFGLAT_PAIRS: 2.9682 2.9682 2.9683
TTBENCH_CFGLAT_DIFF: 0.0000 -0.0001

  DIFFERENCE 0.000, BELOW THE 0.5 CYCLE/PAIR FLOOR against both baselines.
  ConfigurationUnit.md predicts >= 1, so this is the NULL and not a small
  value. EXPECTED against tt-sim, which reads Blackhole's STALLWAIT
  condition mask as 12 bits (raw 11:0, tt_sim/pe/tensix/backends/sync.py
  `_read_wait_res`) where the ISA doc gives 13, so C12 never survives the
  decode and the wait degrades to the 0x7F `all resources` fallback. On a
  card it means the construction did not reach the quantity.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
phase A: the wrong-condition control (slots 20/21, TRISC_CFG)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  variant thr    rdcfg/pair    base/pair   difference
  t1      1           2.968        2.968       -0.000

TTBENCH_CFGLAT_WRONGBIT: 0.0000
  TRISC_CFG is about the RISCV core's outstanding memory requests, not
  about the Configuration Unit's pipeline, so ~0 here is the CORRECT
  reading and is what makes the C12 difference above attributable to the
  condition bit. A control that moved would mean it is not.

